## Milestone 2 becomes the killer feature

Once Milestone 1 works, we build what originally motivated the product:

### Project Change Intelligence

You say:

> We decided to use PostgreSQL rather than MongoDB.

MarkdownGPT searches the project:

```text
Potentially affected documents

technical-architecture.md     HIGH
product-requirements.md       LOW
deployment.md                 MEDIUM
vision.md                     NONE
```

Then:

> **3 changes proposed**

And you get diffs.

That's when MarkdownGPT starts becoming something substantially different from ChatGPT + a Markdown editor.

---

## Milestone 3

Then I'd introduce:

**Project Intelligence**

Semantic search, embeddings, decisions, contradiction detection, outdated-information detection, terminology consistency, document relationships, etc.

So the roadmap becomes very clean:

```text
M1
AI Project Workspace
        ↓
M2
Project Change Intelligence
        ↓
M3
Project Knowledge Intelligence
        ↓
M4
Integrations / Collaboration
```

And now we're finally in a good position to write `technical-architecture.md`.

Because instead of trying to architect some hypothetical finished MarkdownGPT, we can design an architecture that gets **M1 running quickly without boxing us out of M2/M3**.

For the stack, I'm already leaning toward the same pattern you were considering earlier:

```text
Next.js
   │
FastAPI
   │
PostgreSQL
   │
LLM provider abstraction
```

with S3-compatible object storage added when we actually need binary uploads/exports, and vector search added when M2/M3 makes it necessary.

